title: Genesis 3 – The Fall
description: A young adult Sunday school walk through Genesis 3: the serpent’s question, the first sin, the cover-up, the curses, the first promise of a Deliverer, and the expulsion from Eden.
output: lessons/genesis/genesis-3-the-fall.html

# Converted from the old one-page lesson, card for card, in the author's order. The "Adam's Choice – Romans 5"
# pop-up of the old page follows the Genesis 3:6 slide, where its button sat.

=== Introduction
--- Genesis Chapter 3 [title]
overline: Young Adult Sunday School · Genesis Series
heading: Genesis Chapter 3
sub: The Fall • The Curse • The First Promise
hint: Use the arrow keys or swipe to move through the lesson. Tap any gold reference to read the verse.

=== The Temptation
--- “Yea, Hath God Said?” Planting Doubt in God’s Word
kicker: v. 1 · The Serpent’s Opening Move
scripture: Genesis 3:1 | mark: Yea, hath God said, Ye shall not eat of every tree of the garden?
p: The serpent does not begin with a lie; he begins with a question. He does not deny God’s word; he causes Eve to doubt it. The first weapon of the enemy is not atheism but uncertainty about what God has said. [[2 Corinthians 11:3]]

--- The Lie: “Ye Shall Not Surely Die”
kicker: vv. 2–5 · The Appeal, Become Like God
scripture: Genesis 3:2-5 | mark: And the serpent said unto the woman, Ye shall not surely die:; and ye shall be as gods, knowing good and evil.
p: The serpent’s appeal: you are being held back. God is withholding something good from you. You can be as God. Pride was the first sin in heaven ([[Isaiah 14:13-14|Isa. 14:13–14]]); the same bait is set for man.

--- She Saw • She Took • She Gave: He Did Eat
kicker: v. 6 · The Lust of the Eyes, Eve’s Choice, Then Adam’s
scripture: Genesis 3:6 | mark: saw; pleasant to the eyes,; gave also unto her husband with her; and he did eat.
p: Eve was deceived: she convinced herself through three appeals. Good for food (lust of the flesh), pleasant to the eyes (lust of the eyes), desired to make wise (pride of life): [[1 John 2:16]]. Adam was NOT deceived: [[1 Timothy 2:14|1 Tim. 2:14]]. He received God’s command directly before Eve was created: [[Genesis 2:16-17|Gen. 2:16–17]]. Adam chose sin with open eyes.

=== Adam’s Choice: Romans 5
--- Adam’s Choice: Death Through One Man, Life Through One Man
kicker: Cross References · Romans 5
fig: Romans 5:12 | Romans 5:12 | Sin entered through Adam’s wilful choice. He was the federal head of the human race. His act condemned all who come from him.
fig: Romans 5:14 | Romans 5:14 | Adam is called a “figure,” a type, of Christ. The first Adam plunged the race into death; the Last Adam would lift it back to life.

--- The “much more” of grace
fig: Romans 5:17 | Romans 5:17 | The “much more” of grace: what Adam lost, Christ restores in abundance. Death reigned through Adam; the redeemed shall reign in life through Christ.
fig: Romans 5:18–19 | Romans 5:18-19 | The remedy is perfectly shaped to match the wound. One act of disobedience: condemnation. One act of obedience at the cross: justification.

--- In Adam, or in Christ
fig: 1 Corinthians 15:21–22 | 1 Corinthians 15:21-22 | Every human being stands in one of two federal heads: in Adam (dead), or in Christ (alive). There is no neutral ground.
fig: 1 Timothy 2:14 | 1 Timothy 2:14 | Eve was deceived. Adam was not. Adam chose to follow his wife into sin with full knowledge of God’s command. His representative role is therefore the greater.

--- One man representing many
p: Adam received the command directly from God before Eve existed. He was not deceived; he sinned deliberately. This is why Scripture assigns the Fall to Adam, not Eve. But the glory of the gospel is that the same principle that condemned us, one man representing many, is the very mechanism God uses to save us. In Adam, all die. In Christ, all who believe are made alive.

=== The Cover-Up
--- Fig Leaves: Man’s Attempt to Cover His Own Sin
kicker: v. 7 · Their Own Works, Insufficient Before a Holy God
scripture: Genesis 3:7 | mark: and they sewed fig leaves together, and made themselves aprons.
p: Man’s first religious instinct after sin: cover yourself by your own works. Fig leaves could not atone. No human effort, religion, or righteousness can cover the guilt of sin before a holy God. [[Isaiah 64:6|Isa. 64:6]]

--- “Where Art Thou?” God Comes Seeking the Sinner
kicker: vv. 8–10 · The {Lord} God Walking, They Hid
scripture: Genesis 3:8-10 | mark: the voice of the LORD God walking in the garden in the cool of the day; Where art thou?
p: God knew exactly where Adam was. The question is not for God’s information; it is for Adam’s conviction. God is the one who comes seeking the sinner. This is the gospel pattern from the very beginning. [[Luke 19:10]]

--- Adam Blames God. Eve Blames the Serpent. All Are Guilty.
kicker: vv. 11–13 · The Blame Game, No One Takes Responsibility
scripture: Genesis 3:11-13 | mark: The woman whom thou gavest to be with me, she gave me of the tree, and I did eat.; The serpent beguiled me, and I did eat.
p: Adam blames the woman, and subtly blames God who gave her. Eve blames the serpent. But God holds each accountable in turn. We are each guilty of our own choices. [[Romans 14:12|Rom. 14:12]] • [[Ezekiel 18:20|Ezek. 18:20]]

=== The Judgment of God
--- The Proto-Evangelium: The Seed of the Woman Shall Bruise His Head
kicker: vv. 14–15 · The Serpent Cursed, The First Prophecy of Christ
scripture: Genesis 3:14-15 | mark: Because thou hast done this, thou art cursed above all cattle, and above every beast of the field; upon thy belly shalt thou go, and dust shalt thou eat all the days of thy life:

--- The very first word of gospel
p: The very first word of gospel in all Scripture. Before one curse falls on man, God announces the remedy. The seed of the woman, not of a man, points to the virgin birth. [[Galatians 4:4|Gal. 4:4]]
p: He shall bruise thy head: the fatal, final blow at the cross and resurrection. [[Colossians 2:15|Col. 2:15]] • [[Romans 16:20|Rom. 16:20]]
p: Thou shalt bruise his heel: the suffering of Christ. Final end of the serpent: [[Revelation 20:10|Rev. 20:10]]

--- Sorrow in Childbirth • Desire and Rule
kicker: v. 16 · Eve Cursed, and All Women
scripture: Genesis 3:16 | mark: I will greatly multiply thy sorrow and thy conception; in sorrow thou shalt bring forth children
p: The curse falls on the role God designed: childbearing becomes sorrow. The creation order of male headship is now complicated by the effects of sin. Every woman who has ever suffered in childbirth bears the mark of the Fall. Hope: [[1 Timothy 2:15|1 Tim. 2:15]]

--- Thorns and Thistles • Sweat • Dust to Dust
kicker: vv. 17–19 · Adam Cursed, and All Men
scripture: Genesis 3:17-19 | mark: cursed is the ground for thy sake; Thorns also and thistles shall it bring forth to thee; till thou return unto the ground
p: Physical death enters here; every grave is the direct consequence of this moment. Every man who has ever broken his back for daily bread bears the mark of the Fall. The thorns Adam now cultivates foreshadow the crown of thorns on the Last Adam: Christ bore the curse in full. [[Galatians 3:13|Gal. 3:13]] • [[Romans 5:12|Rom. 5:12]]

=== The Gospel Enacted
--- Blood Must Be Shed: God Clothes the Sinner
kicker: v. 21 · The {Lord} Makes Coats of Skins
scripture: Genesis 3:21
p: Man covered himself with leaves: his own works. God replaced those leaves with skins. An animal had to die. Blood had to be shed. This is the first sacrifice in Scripture, and it is God who performs it. God himself provides the covering for sin at the cost of innocent life. [[Hebrews 9:22|Heb. 9:22]] • [[John 1:29]] • [[Isaiah 61:10|Isa. 61:10]]

=== Spiritual Death: Cast Out
--- Expelled: Separated from God’s Presence
kicker: vv. 22–24 · Driven Out • The Flaming Sword • The Tree of Life Guarded
scripture: Genesis 3:22-24 | mark: Therefore the LORD God sent him forth from the garden of Eden, to till the ground from whence he was taken.; So he drove out the man; and he placed at the east of the garden of Eden Cherubims, and a flaming sword which turned every way, to keep the way of the tree of life.
p: Spiritual death: separation from the presence of God where He walked with man. The way to the tree of life is now barred. It will not be opened again until the cross tears the veil ([[Matthew 27:51|Matt. 27:51]]), and the last chapter of Scripture restores what was lost: [[Revelation 22:14|Rev. 22:14]]

=== The Whole Story
--- What the Fall Cost, What Christ Restores
kicker: Genesis 3 in One Frame
p: Man doubted God’s word. Man desired to be God. Man chose sin. Man tried to cover himself. Man hid from God. Man blamed others. Man was cursed. Man was driven out.
p: But before the first curse was pronounced, God announced a Deliverer. Before the first animal died, God showed that blood would cover sin. Before the gate closed, God was already planning to open it again.
big: Romans 5:19
